IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 12 (relationship of statutory sick pay with benefits and other payments) and SCHEDULE 13 (relationship of statutory maternity pay with benefits and other payments).
-- The converter dropped the paragraph numbers. Schedule 12 has six headings: 1 The general principle, 2 Contractual remuneration, 3 Incapacity benefit, then an unheaded
-- paragraph 4 (the "(1) Where a period of entitlement ... comes to an end" paragraph that paragraph 3(1) names as "paragraph 4 below"), 5 Incapacity benefit for widows and widowers,
-- 6 Unemployability supplement. Schedule 13 has three: 1 The general principle, 2 Incapacity benefit, 3 Contractual remuneration (3(2A) is cited in the text).
-- Schedule 13 paragraph 3(2A) takes "week" from the day the maternity pay period begins: the core's fourth `Week convention`.

§ `Schedule 12 -- relationship of statutory sick pay with benefits and other payments`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- the general principle`

-- 1: a day which (a) is a day of incapacity for work in relation to any contract of service and (b) falls within a period of entitlement (whether or not it is also a qualifying day)
-- "shall not be treated for the purposes of this Act as a day of incapacity for work for the purposes of determining whether a period is ... a period of incapacity for work for
-- the purposes of incapacity benefit".
-- src:5697 | Any day which—
-- src:5698 | (a) is a day of incapacity for work in relation to any contract of service; and
-- src:5699 | (b) falls within a period of entitlement (whether or not it is also a qualifying day),
-- src:5700 | shall not be treated for the purposes of this Act as a day of incapacity for work for the purposes of determining whether a period is ... a period of incapacity for work for the purposes of incapacity benefit.
@ref sch 12 para 1 (src:5697-5700)
GIVEN `the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day falls within a period of entitlement to statutory sick pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 1 the day counts as a day of incapacity for work for incapacity benefit` MEANS
    IF `the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to a contract of service` AND `the day falls within a period of entitlement to statutory sick pay`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be treated ... as a day of incapacity for work for the purposes of determining whether a period is ... a period of incapacity for work for the purposes of incapacity benefit"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks only of a day within (a) and (b)

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- contractual remuneration`

-- 2(1) and (2)(b): any entitlement to statutory sick pay "shall not affect any right of an employee in relation to remuneration under any contract of service", subject to (2) and (3);
-- and statutory sick pay paid for a day of incapacity "shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration to that employee in respect of that day".
-- So the contractual remuneration still owed for the day is the liability less the statutory sick pay paid for it, and not below nothing.
-- src:5702 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) below, any entitlement to statutory sick pay shall not affect any right of an employee in relation to remuneration under any contract of service (“contractual remuneration”).
-- src:5703 | (2) Subject to sub-paragraph (3) below—
-- src:5704 | (a) any contractual remuneration paid to an employee by an employer of his in respect of a day of incapacity for work shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory sick pay to that employee in respect of that day; and
-- src:5705 | (b) any statutory sick pay paid by an employer to an employee of his in respect of a day of incapacity for work shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration to that employee in respect of that day.
@ref sch 12 para 2(1) and (2)(b) (src:5702-5705)
GIVEN `the employer's liability to pay contractual remuneration for the day` IS A NUMBER
      `the statutory sick pay the employer paid for the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 12 para 2(2)(b) the contractual remuneration still owed for the day` MEANS
    max 0 (`the employer's liability to pay contractual remuneration for the day` MINUS `the statutory sick pay the employer paid for the day`)

-- 2(2)(a): contractual remuneration paid for a day of incapacity for work "shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory sick pay to that employee in respect of that day".
-- (3): regulations may say which payments are, and are not, contractual remuneration (inert, machinery).
-- src:5703 | (2) Subject to sub-paragraph (3) below—
-- src:5704 | (a) any contractual remuneration paid to an employee by an employer of his in respect of a day of incapacity for work shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory sick pay to that employee in respect of that day; and
@ref sch 12 para 2(2)(a) (src:5703-5704)
GIVEN `the employer's liability to pay statutory sick pay for the day` IS A NUMBER
      `the contractual remuneration the employer paid for the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 12 para 2(2)(a) the statutory sick pay still owed for the day` MEANS
    max 0 (`the employer's liability to pay statutory sick pay for the day` MINUS `the contractual remuneration the employer paid for the day`)

§§ `Paragraphs 3 and 4 -- incapacity benefit after a period of entitlement ends`

-- 3(1): "This paragraph and paragraph 4 below have effect to exclude, where a period of entitlement ... comes to an end, the provisions by virtue of which short-term incapacity benefit is not paid
-- for the first three days." A statement of what 3 and 4 do, with no condition of its own: it is cited with the rule below that does it (3(2) and (3)), and with 4(1) and (2).
-- 3(2) and (3): if the first day immediately after the day on which the period of entitlement ended (a) is a day of incapacity for work in relation to the employee and (b) is not a day to which
-- paragraph 1 applies by reason of entitlement as between the employee and another employer, that day shall, except in prescribed cases, be or form part of a period of incapacity for work notwithstanding
-- section 30C(1)(b) (which makes a period of incapacity for work at least 4 days long). Where each of the first two, or first three, consecutive days meets (a) and (b), the second, or the second and third, days
-- are treated as the first is.
-- src:5708 | (1) This paragraph and paragraph 4 below have effect to exclude, where a period of entitlement as between an employee and an employer of his comes to an end, the provisions by virtue of which short-term incapacity benefit is not paid for the first three days.
-- src:5709 | (2) If the first day immediately following the day on which the period of entitlement came to an end—
-- src:5710 | (a) is a day of incapacity for work in relation to that employee, and
-- src:5711 | (b) is not a day in relation to which paragraph 1 above applies by reason of any entitlement as between the employee and another employer,
-- src:5712 | that day shall, except in prescribed cases, be or form part of a period of incapacity for work notwithstanding section 30C(1)(b) above (by virtue of which a period of incapacity for work must be at least 4 days long).
-- src:5713 | (3) Where each of the first two consecutive days, or the first three consecutive days, following the day on which the period of entitlement came to an end is a day to which paragraphs (a) and (b) of sub-paragraph (2) above apply, that sub-paragraph has effect in relation to the second day or, as the case may be, in relation to the second and third days, as it has effect in relation to the first.
@ref sch 12 para 3(1), (2) and (3) (src:5708-5713)
GIVEN `the number of the day counted from the day after the period of entitlement came to an end` IS A NUMBER
      `every day from the first to this one meets paragraphs (a) and (b) of sub-paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a prescribed case in which the sub-paragraph does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 3(2) the day is or forms part of a period of incapacity for work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the number of the day counted from the day after the period of entitlement came to an end` LESS THAN 1) OR (`the number of the day counted from the day after the period of entitlement came to an end` GREATER THAN 3)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the first day" and "each of the first two consecutive days, or the first three" name no other day
        IF (`the number of the day counted from the day after the period of entitlement came to an end` EQUALS 1) AND (NOT `every day from the first to this one meets paragraphs (a) and (b) of sub-paragraph (2)`)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the first day immediately following the day on which the period of entitlement came to an end— (a) is a day of incapacity for work ..., and (b) is not a day in relation to which paragraph 1 above applies" (a failed "if")
        IF NOT `every day from the first to this one meets paragraphs (a) and (b) of sub-paragraph (2)`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sub-paragraph (3) is introduced by "Where each of the first two consecutive days, or the first three consecutive days, ... is a day to which paragraphs (a) and (b) ... apply", a "where", not an "if"
        IF `it is a prescribed case in which the sub-paragraph does not apply`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except in prescribed cases"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 4(1) (the unnumbered paragraph that 3(1) calls "paragraph 4 below"): where a period of entitlement comes to an end, section 30A(3) (exclusion of benefit for the first 3 days of a period) "does not apply in relation to any day which
-- (a) is or forms part of a period of incapacity for work (whether by virtue of paragraph 3 above or otherwise), and (b) falls within the period of 57 days immediately following the day on which the period of entitlement came to an end".
-- src:5714 | (1) Where a period of entitlement as between an employee and an employer of his comes to an end, section 30A(3) above (exclusion of benefit for first 3 days of period) does not apply in relation to any day which—
-- src:5715 | (a) is or forms part of a period of incapacity for work (whether by virtue of paragraph 3 above or otherwise), and
-- src:5716 | (b) falls within the period of 57 days immediately following the day on which the period of entitlement came to an end.
@ref sch 12 para 4(1) (src:5714-5716)
GIVEN `the day is or forms part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period of entitlement came to an end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 4(1) section 30A(3) does not apply to the day` MEANS
    IF `the day is or forms part of a period of incapacity for work` AND ((Day day) MINUS (Day `the day on which the period of entitlement came to an end`) AT LEAST 1) AND ((Day day) MINUS (Day `the day on which the period of entitlement came to an end`) AT MOST 57)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply in relation to any day which (a) ... and (b) ..." says nothing of other days

-- 4(2): where 4(1) applies to a day, section 30A(3) "does not apply in relation to any later day in the same period of incapacity for work".
-- src:5717 | (2) Where sub-paragraph (1) above applies in relation to a day, section 30A(3) above does not apply in relation to any later day in the same period of incapacity for work.
@ref sch 12 para 4(2) (src:5717)
GIVEN `sub-paragraph (1) applies to an earlier day in the same period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 4(2) section 30A(3) does not apply to the later day` MEANS
    IF `sub-paragraph (1) applies to an earlier day in the same period of incapacity for work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where sub-paragraph (1) above applies in relation to a day"

§§ `Paragraphs 5 and 6 -- incapacity benefit for widows and widowers; unemployability supplement`

-- 5: "Paragraph 1 above does not apply for the purpose of determining whether the conditions specified in section 40(3) or (4) or section 41(2) or (3) above are satisfied."
-- src:5719 | Paragraph 1 above does not apply for the purpose of determining whether the conditions specified in section 40(3) or (4) or section 41(2) or (3) above are satisfied.
@ref sch 12 para 5 (src:5719)
GIVEN `the purpose is determining whether the conditions specified in section 40(3) or (4) or section 41(2) or (3) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 5 paragraph 1 applies` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is determining whether the conditions specified in section 40(3) or (4) or section 41(2) or (3) are satisfied`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 1 above does not apply for the purpose of determining whether the conditions ... are satisfied"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says only that paragraph 1 does not apply for that purpose

-- 6: "Paragraph 1 above does not apply in relation to paragraph 3 of Schedule 7 to this Act and accordingly the references in paragraph 3 of that Schedule to a period of interruption of employment
-- shall be construed as if the provisions re-enacted in this Part of this Act had not been enacted."
-- src:5721 | Paragraph 1 above does not apply in relation to paragraph 3 of Schedule 7 to this Act and accordingly the references in paragraph 3 of that Schedule to a period of interruption of employment shall be construed as if the provisions re-enacted in this Part of this Act had not been enacted.
@ref sch 12 para 6 (src:5721)
GIVEN `the purpose is paragraph 3 of Schedule 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 6 paragraph 1 applies` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is paragraph 3 of Schedule 7`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 1 above does not apply in relation to paragraph 3 of Schedule 7 to this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says only that paragraph 1 does not apply for that purpose

§ `Schedule 13 -- relationship of statutory maternity pay with benefits and other payments`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- the general principle`

-- 1: "Except as may be prescribed, a day which falls within the maternity pay period shall not be treated as a day of incapacity for work for the purposes of determining, for this Act, whether it forms
-- part of a period of incapacity for work for the purposes of incapacity benefit."
-- src:5724 | Except as may be prescribed, a day which falls within the maternity pay period shall not be treated as a day of incapacity for work for the purposes of determining, for this Act, whether it forms part of a period of incapacity for work for the purposes of incapacity benefit.
@ref sch 13 para 1 (src:5724)
GIVEN `the day falls within the maternity pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations prescribe otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 1 the day counts as a day of incapacity for work for incapacity benefit` MEANS
    IF `the day falls within the maternity pay period` AND NOT `regulations prescribe otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a day which falls within the maternity pay period shall not be treated as a day of incapacity for work"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks only of a day within the maternity pay period

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- incapacity benefit`

-- 2(1): regulations may provide that in prescribed circumstances a day in the maternity pay period is treated as a day of incapacity for work for the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit or
-- long-term incapacity benefit (inert, machinery).
-- 2(2): regulations may provide that an amount equal to a woman's statutory maternity pay for a period is deducted from the benefit for the same period and she is entitled to the benefit only if there is a
-- balance, at a weekly rate equal to it. Where the regulations do provide it, the rate is the benefit less the statutory maternity pay, and nothing if there is no balance.
-- src:5727 | (2) Regulations may provide that an amount equal to a woman’s statutory maternity pay for a period shall be deducted from any such benefit in respect of the same period and a woman shall be entitled to such benefit only if there is a balance after the deduction and, if there is such a balance, at a weekly rate equal to it.
@ref sch 13 para 2(2) (src:5727)
GIVEN `regulations provide for the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly amount of the woman's statutory maternity pay for the same period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 13 para 2(2) the weekly rate of the benefit after the deduction` MEANS
    IF `regulations provide for the deduction`
    THEN max 0 (`the weekly rate of the benefit` MINUS `the weekly amount of the woman's statutory maternity pay for the same period`)
    ELSE `the weekly rate of the benefit`

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- contractual remuneration`

-- 3(2A): "week" means "a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the maternity pay period begins": the core's fourth `Week convention`.
-- src:5733 | (2A) In sub-paragraph (2) “week” means a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the maternity pay period begins.
@ref sch 13 para 3(2A) (src:5733)
GIVETH A `Week convention`
`sch 13 para 3(2A) the meaning of week` MEANS `a period of 7 days beginning with the day on which a stated period begins`

-- 3(1) and (2)(b): any entitlement to statutory maternity pay "shall not affect any right of a woman in relation to remuneration under any contract of service", subject to (2) and (3); and
-- statutory maternity pay paid for a week in the maternity pay period "shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration to her in respect of that week".
-- src:5729 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) below, any entitlement to statutory maternity pay shall not affect any right of a woman in relation to remuneration under any contract of service (“contractual remuneration”).
-- src:5730 | (2) Subject to sub-paragraph (3) below—
-- src:5731 | (a) any contractual remuneration paid to a woman by an employer of hers in respect of a week in the maternity pay period shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory maternity pay to her in respect of that week; and
-- src:5732 | (b) any statutory maternity pay paid by an employer to a woman who is an employee of his in respect of a week in the maternity pay period shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration to her in respect of that week.
@ref sch 13 para 3(1) and (2)(b) (src:5729-5732)
GIVEN `the employer's liability to pay contractual remuneration for the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the statutory maternity pay the employer paid for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 13 para 3(2)(b) the contractual remuneration still owed for the week` MEANS
    max 0 (`the employer's liability to pay contractual remuneration for the week` MINUS `the statutory maternity pay the employer paid for the week`)

-- 3(2)(a): contractual remuneration paid to a woman for a week in the maternity pay period "shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory maternity pay to her in respect of that week".
-- 3(3): regulations may say which payments are, and are not, contractual remuneration (inert, machinery).
-- src:5730 | (2) Subject to sub-paragraph (3) below—
-- src:5731 | (a) any contractual remuneration paid to a woman by an employer of hers in respect of a week in the maternity pay period shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory maternity pay to her in respect of that week; and
@ref sch 13 para 3(2)(a) (src:5730-5731)
GIVEN `the employer's liability to pay statutory maternity pay for the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the contractual remuneration the employer paid for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 13 para 3(2)(a) the statutory maternity pay still owed for the week` MEANS
    max 0 (`the employer's liability to pay statutory maternity pay for the week` MINUS `the contractual remuneration the employer paid for the week`)
